// PARAM: --analysis interval
// Permanent regression for the certified Interval widening backend
// (docs/... the warrowing/widening solver bridge fixed for issue #96):
// before that fix, this two-line self-referential global write could make
// the join-only Interval backend diverge, because the side-effecting
// global-summary constraint for `total` folded the write's result back into
// its own current value -- a fixpoint dependency that exists even without
// any source-level loop.
//
// Base-style migration acceptance case: `total` now lives in the same
// reachability-lifted local unknown as every local, so there is no
// separate flow-insensitive global summary for its write to fold back
// into in the first place. Termination and precision now coincide -- the
// mechanism that used to cost both is gone, not merely worked around.
global total;
void main() {
  total := 0;
  total := total + 3;
  __voblint_check(0 < total) // PROVED
}
